※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4520

※ Where the divisor is written down the operator answers a truth value, there
※ being no pair of operands it has no answer for -- except this one.  A divisor
※ the program works out may turn out to be zero and the answer is a result,
※ which has somewhere to say so; a zero written down has nowhere, and a program
※ that wrote one asked a question it knew the answer to.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = 7u8
    if 0u8 ∣ n:
        0u6
    else:
        1u6
